  "strategy": "Approach and rationale:\nThe goal is to minimize the maximum overlap between a step function h(x) and its shifted version. Current approaches have not achieved the desired lower bound of 0.380876 despite previous lower bounds around 0.381096. The current strategy uses spatial transformations not just parameter perturbations to explore the solution space more thoroughly. By introducing significant morphological deformations, we can escape local optima that resist improvement. Each perturbation operation during local optimization should not be a minor disturbance but a meaningful structural change to the function's shape.\n\nMathematical specification:\nThe problem: minimize C\u2085 = max_k \u27e9<h|h+k\u27e9 where h+k is the shifted function. Formally, the objective is:\nL(h) = max{ \u222b h(x)(1-h(x+k)) dx for all k }\nsubject to:\n\u222b h(x) dx = 1 and 0 \u2264 h(x) \u2264 1 for all x \u2208 [0,2]\n\nThe transformation-based approach:\n1. Represent h as an array of n samples on [0,2].\n2. Maintain the integral constraint through repair mechanisms: scale(clip(compress_balance(...))\n3. Apply inversion-based transforms that change the function's global structure rather than local details.\n\nThese transforms:\n1. Rotate phases: find a \"mutation center\" (local minimum) and invert the function locally.\n2. Hybrid thresholds: transform continuous values to two-level values at strategic points.\n3. Windowed shifting: apply adaptive shrink/expansions to segments defined by thresholds.\n\nImplementation procedure:\n\n1. Initialization:\n- Start with initial_h_values with n=360 samples\n- Set n_points = min(1440, available_time * samples_per_second * 2)\n\n2. Parent management:\n- Preserve closest valid parent from previous generation\n- Repair: normalise \u2192 clip to [0,1] \u2192 scale if integral not 1\n\n3. Correlation computation:\n- Use provided compute_C5(h) method\n- Store trajectory to enforce bipartite validation\n\n4. Local optimization loop per resolution:\n- Tentative expansions: twice current size\n- Acceptance: only if strictly better than local best\n\n5. Novel perturbations:\ndef rotate_phase_shift(h):\n    \"\"\"Locally invert to phase-rotate probability density\"\"\"\n    Find threshold (local min point)\n    Mirror subarray around threshold\n    Repair result with adaptive normalization\n\ndef hybrid_threshold(h, rate):\n    \"\"\"Convert to two-level representation with preserved integral\"\"\"\n    Select fraction 'rate' for conversion\n    Partition sorted indices into two-level curve\n    Optimize binary decision boundary\n\ndef adaptive_window_shift(h, expansion):\n    \"\"\"Shrink portions with high probability to boost coverage\"\"\"\n    Compute derivative magnitudes\n    Isolate windows based on threshold crossings\n    Non-uniform expansion in selected regions\n\n6. Random components:\n- Keep some Gaussian noise (decaying standard deviation)\n- Previous strategies maintained key structural markers\n\n7. Termination:\nIf compute time < 1/6 remaining:\n    Trigger \"limp-mode\" optimization\n    Return best-known valid configuration\n\nSearch choices and variations:\n- Use rate = n_points_minor/initial_n scaling\n- Steps: [(0.6, 1000), (0.8, 800), (1.2, 600)]\n- Always enable four structural-transform-based directions\n- Use recursive deep dives for improving positions\n\nCompute budget and robustness:\n- n_points scaling: three iterations (360 \u2192 720 \u2192 1440 samples)\n- Each optimization: 500 iterations\n- Monitor compute time per resolution\n- Fallback: preserve original h at all stages\n\nValidation and return contract:\n1. Final check: \n   compute_C5(h) must be below current best\n   np.all(0 <= h <= 1) must hold\n   integral condition: |sum(h)*dx - 1| < 1e-5\n2. Metrics: C\u2085, h_with_n_points, C\u2085_history\n3. Restart triggers after 100 worse steps\n4. Use single-precision floating-point internally, exact double only for storage",
